WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.932
Node functions are still ordinary Python.

00:00:02.932 --> 00:00:09.787
The retrieve node reads state, retrieves documents, and returns only the fields it changes:

00:00:09.787 --> 00:00:13.382
the new documents and an increased step count.

00:00:13.382 --> 00:00:17.903
The routing function grades the evidence and then applies the correction budget.

00:00:18.583 --> 00:00:22.490
If the score passes the threshold, return generate.

00:00:22.490 --> 00:00:28.085
If the score is weak but the maximum step count has been reached, return stop.

00:00:28.085 --> 00:00:30.581
Otherwise, return rewrite.

00:00:31.145 --> 00:00:34.452
This is the same policy we wrote in plain Python.

00:00:34.452 --> 00:00:37.412
Lang Graph has not changed the algorithm.

00:00:37.412 --> 00:00:40.067
It has made the transitions explicit.

00:00:40.067 --> 00:00:45.522
Good evidence generates. Weak evidence corrects only while budget remains.

00:00:45.522 --> 00:00:47.694
Exhausted budget stops.
